e arguments is null\");\n76:         // it would be better that we don't need the container to get the target\n77:         // this constructor can be without parameters as soon as we improve\n78:         // targetChanged\n79:         _clearable = clearable;\n80:         _propertySetName = propertySetName;\n81:     }\n82:     \n83:     \n84: \n85:     /**\n86:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#listRoleItemSet(MElementEvent)\n87:      */\n88:     public void listRoleItemSet(MElementEvent e) {\n89:     }\n90: \n91:     /**\n92:      * If the property that this comboboxmodel depicts is changed by the NSUML\n93:      * model, this method will make sure that it is changed in the comboboxmodel\n94:      * too.\n95:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#propertySet(MElementEvent)\n96:      */\n97:     public void propertySet(MElementEvent e) {\n98:         if (e.getName().equals(_propertySetName) \n99:             && e.getSource() == getTarget() && \n100:             (contains(getChangedElement(e)) || getChangedElement(e) == null)) {\n101:                 setSelectedItem(getChangedElement(e));\n102:         }\n103:     }\n104: \n105:     /**\n106:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#recovered(MElementEvent)\n107:      */\n108:     public void recovered(MElementEvent e) {\n109:     }\n110: \n111:     /**\n112:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#removed(MElementEvent)\n113:      */\n114:     public void removed(MElementEvent e) {\n115:         if (contains(getChangedElement(e))) {\n116:             Object o = getChangedElement(e);\n117:             if (o instanceof Collection) {\n118:                 removeAll((Collection)o);\n119:             } else {\n120:                 removeElement(o);\n121:             }      \n122:         }\n123:     }\n124: \n125:     /**\n126:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#roleAdded(MElementEvent)\n127:      */\n128:     public void roleAdded(MElementEvent e) {\n129:         if (isValidEvent(e)) {\n130:             Object o = getChangedElement(e);\n131:             if (o instanceof Collection) { // this should not happen but\n132:                     // you never know with NSUML\n133:                 log.warn(\"Collection added via roleAdded! The correct element\" +\n134:                     \"is probably not selected...\");\n135:                 Iterator it = ((Collection)o).iterator();\n136:                 while(it.hasNext()) {\n137:                     Object o2 = it.next();\n138:                     addElement(it.next());                    \n139:                 }\n140:             } else {\n141:                 addElement(o);\n142:             }\n143:         }\n144:     }\n145: \n146:     /**\n147:      * @see ru.novosoft.uml.MElementListener#roleRemoved(MElementEvent)\n148:      */\n149:     public void roleRemoved(MElementEvent e) {\n150:         if (contains(getChangedElement(e))) {\n151:             Object o = getChangedElement(e);\n152:             if (o instanceof Collection) {\n153:                 removeAll((Collection)o);\n154:             } else {\n155:                 removeElement(o);\n156:             }      \n157:         }\n158:     }\n159:     \n160:     public void targetChanged(Object newTarget) {\n161:         setTarget(newTarget);\n162:     }\n163: \n164:     public void targetReasserted(Object newTarget) {\n165:         setTarget(newTarget);\n166:     }\n167:     \n168:     /**\n169:      * Returns true if the given element is valid, i.e. it may be added to the \n170:      * list of elements.\n171:      * @param element\n172:      */\n173:     protected abstract boolean isValidElement(MBase element);\n174:     \n175:     /**\n176:      * Builds the list of elements and sets the selectedIndex to the currently \n177:      * selected item if there is one. Called from targetChanged every time the \n178:      * target of the proppanel is changed.\n179:      */\n180:     protected abstract void buildModelList();\n181:  \n182:  \n183:     /**\n184:      * Utility method to change all elements in the list with modelelements\n185:      * at once.\n186:      * @param elements\n187:      */\n188:     protected void setElements(Collection elements) {\n189:         if (elements != null) {\n190:             removeAllElements();\n191:             addAll(elements);\n192:             if (_clearable && !elements.contains(\"\")) {\n193:                 addElement(\"\");\n194:             }\n195:         } else\n196:             throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"In setElements: may not set \" +\n197:                 \"elements to null collection\");\n198:     }\n199:     \n200:     /**\n201:      * Utility method to get the target. Sets the _target if the _target is null\n202:      * via the method setTarget().\n203:      * @return MModelElement\n204:      */\n205:     protected Object getTarget() {\n206:         return _target;\n207:     }\n208:     \n209:     /**\n210:      * Utility method to remove a collection of elements from the model\n211:      * @param col\n212:      */\n213:     protected void removeAll(Collection col) {\n214:         // we don't want to mark to many elements as changed. \n215:         // therefore we don't directly call removeall on the list\n216:         Iterator it = col.iterator();\n217:         while (it.hasNext()) {\n218:             removeElement(it.next());\n219:         }\n220:     }\n221:     \n222:     /**\n223:      * Utility method to add a collection of elements to the model\n224:      * @param col\n225:      */\n226:     protected void addAll(Collection col) {\n227:         Iterator it = col.iterator();\n228:         Object o2 = getSelectedItem();\n229:         while (it.hasNext()) {\n230:             Object o = it.next();\n231:             addElement(o);\n232:         }\n233:         setSelectedItem(o2);\n234:     }\n235:     \n236:     \n237:     \n238:     /**\n239:      * Utility method to get the changed element from some event e\n240:      * @param e\n241:    