ired height is bigger, then the additional height is\n898:      * equally distributed among all figs (i.e. compartments), such that the\n899:      * cumulated height of all visible figs equals the demanded height<p>.\n900:      *\n901:      * Some of this has \"magic numbers\" hardcoded in. In particular there is\n902:      * a knowledge that the minimum height of a name compartment is 21\n903:      * pixels.<p>\n904:      *\n905:      * @param x  Desired X coordinate of upper left corner\n906:      *\n907:      * @param y  Desired Y coordinate of upper left corner\n908:      *\n909:      * @param w  Desired width of the FigClass\n910:      *\n911:      * @param h  Desired height of the FigClass\n912:      */\n913:     protected void setBoundsImpl(final int x, final int y, final int w, final int h) {\n914:         Rectangle oldBounds = getBounds();\n915: \n916:         // set bounds of big box\n917:         getBigPort().setBounds(x, y, w, h);\n918:         borderFig.setBounds(x, y, w, h);\n919: \n920:         // Save our old boundaries (needed later), and get minimum size\n921:         // info. \"whitespace\" will be used to maintain a running calculation of our\n922:         // size at various points.\n923: \n924:         final int whitespace = h - getMinimumSize().height;\n925: \n926:         getNameFig().setLineWidth(0);\n927:         getNameFig().setLineColor(Color.red);\n928:         int currentHeight = 0;\n929: \n930:         if (getStereotypeFig().isVisible()) {\n931:             int stereotypeHeight = getStereotypeFig().getMinimumSize().height;\n932:             getStereotypeFig().setBounds(\n933:                     x,\n934:                     y,\n935:                     w,\n936:                     stereotypeHeight);\n937:             currentHeight = stereotypeHeight;\n938:         }\n939: \n940:         int nameHeight = getNameFig().getMinimumSize().height;\n941:         getNameFig().setBounds(x, y + currentHeight, w, nameHeight);\n942:         currentH