ion\"));\n82:     protected static Action _actionAggregation = new RadioAction(\n83:         new ActionAddAssociation(\n84:             ModelFacade.AGGREGATE_AGGREGATIONKIND,\n85:             false,\n86:             \"Aggregation\"));\n87:     protected static Action _actionComposition = new RadioAction(\n88:         new ActionAddAssociation(\n89:             ModelFacade.COMPOSITE_AGGREGATIONKIND,\n90:             false,\n91:             \"Composition\"));\n92:     protected static Action _actionUniAssociation = new RadioAction(\n93:         new ActionAddAssociation(\n94:             ModelFacade.NONE_AGGREGATIONKIND,\n95:             true,\n96:             \"UniAssociation\"));\n97:     protected static Action _actionUniAggregation = new RadioAction(\n98:         new ActionAddAssociation(\n99:             ModelFacade.AGGREGATE_AGGREGATIONKIND,\n100:             true,\n101:             \"UniAggregation\"));\n102:     protected static Action _actionUniComposition = new RadioAction(\n103:         new ActionAddAssociation(\n104:             ModelFacade.COMPOSITE_AGGREGATIONKIND,\n105:             true,\n106:             \"UniComposition\"));\n107: \n108:     /**\n109:      * Tool to create a generalization between UML artifacts using a\n110:      * polyedge.<p>\n111:      */\n112:     protected static Action _actionGeneralize = new RadioAction(\n113:         new CmdSetMode(\n114:             ModeCreatePolyEdge.class,\n115:             \"edgeClass\",\n116:             ModelFacade.GENERALIZATION,\n117:             \"Generalization\"));\n118: \n119:     /**\n120:      * Tool to create an extend relationship between UML use cases\n121:      * using a polyedge.<p>\n122:      */\n123:     protected static Action _actionExtend = new RadioAction(\n124:         new CmdSetMode(\n125:             ModeCreatePolyEdge.class,\n126:             \"edgeClass\",\n127:             ModelFacade.EXTEND,\n128:             \"Extend\"));\n129: \n130:     /**\n131:      * Tool to create an include relationship between UML use cases\n132:      * using a polyedge.<p>\n133:      */\n134:     protected static Action _actionInclude = new RadioAction(\n135:         new CmdSetMode(\n136:             ModeCreatePolyEdge.class,\n137:             \"edgeClass\",\n138:             ModelFacade.INCLUDE,\n139:             \"Include\"));\n140: \n141:     /**\n142:      * Tool to create a dependency between UML artifacts using a\n143:      * polyedge.<p>\n144:      */\n145:     protected static Action _actionDependency = new RadioAction(\n146:         new CmdSetMode(\n147:             ModeCreatePolyEdge.class,\n148:             \"edgeClass\",\n149:             ModelFacade.DEPENDENCY,\n150:             \"Dependency\"));\n151: \n152:     /**\n153:      * A static counter of the use case index (used in constructing a\n154:      * unique name for each new diagram.<p>\n155:      */\n156:     private static int useCaseDiagramSerial = 1;\n157: \n158:     // constructors\n159: \n160:     /**\n161:      * Construct a new use case diagram with no defined namespace.<p>\n162:      *\n163:      * Note we must never call this directly, since defining the\n164:      * namespace is what makes everything work. However GEF will call\n165:      * it directly when loading a new diagram, so it must remain\n166:      * public.<p>\n167:      *\n168:      * A unique name is constructed by using the serial index\n169:      * {@link #useCaseDiagramSerial}. We allow for the possibility\n170:      * that setting this may fail, in which case no name is set.<p>\n171:      */\n172:     public UMLUseCaseDiagram() {\n173:         try {\n174:             setName(getNewDiagramName());\n175:         } catch (PropertyVetoException pve) { }\n176:     }\n177: \n178:     /**\n179:      * Construct a new use case diagram with in a defined namespace.<p>\n180:      *\n181:      * Invokes the generic constructor {@link #UMLUseCaseDiagram()},\n182:      * then intialises the namespace (which initializes all the\n183:      * graphics).<p>\n184:      *\n185:      * This is the constructor which should always be used.<p>\n186:      *\n187:      * @param m  the desired namespace for this diagram.\n188:      */\n189:     public UMLUseCaseDiagram(Object m) {\n190: \n191:         this();\n192: \n193:         if (!ModelFacade.isANamespace(m))\n194:             throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n195: \n196:         setNamespace(m);\n197:     }\n198: \n199:     /**\n200:      * Constructor \n201:      * @param name the name for the diagram\n202:      * @param namespace the namespace for the diagram\n203:      */\n204:     public UMLUseCaseDiagram(String name, Object namespace) {\n205:         this(namespace);\n206: \n207:         if (!ModelFacade.isANamespace(namespace))\n208:             throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n209: \n210:         try {\n211:             setName(name);\n212:         } catch (PropertyVetoException v) { }\n213:     }\n214: \n215:     /**\n216:      * Perform a number of important initializations of a <em>Use Case\n217:      * Diagram</em>.<p>\n218:      *\n219:      * Creates a new graph model for the diagram, settings its\n220:      * namespace to that supplied.<p>\n221:      *\n222:      * Changed <em>lay</em> from <em>LayerPerspective</em> to\n223:      * <em>LayerPerspectiveMutable</em>. This class is a child of\n224:      * <em>LayerPerspective</em> and was implemented to correct some\n225:      * difficulties in changing the model. <em>lay</em> is used mainly\n226:      * in <em>LayerManager</em>(GEF) to control the adding, changing\n227:      * and deleting of items in a layer of the diagram.<p>\n228:      *\n229:      * Set a renderer suitable for the use case diagram.<p>\n230:      *\n231:      * <em>Note</em>. This is declared as public. Not clear that other\n232:      * classes should be allowed to invoke this method.<p>\n233:      *\n234:      * @param handle Namespace to be used for this diagram.\n235:      *\n236:      * @author   psager@tig