s file version\", e);\n94:         } catch (IOException e) {\n95:             throw new SaveException(\n96:                     \"Failed to archive the previous file version\", e);\n97:         }\n98: \n99:         BufferedWriter writer = null;\n100:         try {\n101:             project.setFile(file);\n102: \n103:             String encoding = \"UTF-8\";\n104:             FileOutputStream stream =\n105:                 new FileOutputStream(file);\n106:             writer =\n107:                 new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(\n108:                         stream, encoding));\n109: \n110:             int size = project.getMembers().size();\n111:             for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n112:                 ProjectMember projectMember =\n113:                     (ProjectMember) project.getMembers().get(i);\n114:                 if (projectMember.getType().equalsIgnoreCase(\"xmi\")) {\n115:                     if (LOG.isInfoEnabled()) {\n116:                         LOG.info(\"Saving member of type: \"\n117:                               + ((ProjectMember) project.getMembers()\n118:                                     .get(i)).getType());\n119:                     }\n120:                     MemberFilePersister persister = null;\n121:                     if (projectMember instanceof ProjectMemberDiagram) {\n122:                         persister = new DiagramMemberFilePersister();\n123:                     } else if (projectMember instanceof ProjectMemberTodoList) {\n124:                         persister = new TodoListMemberFilePersister();\n125:                     } else if (projectMember instanceof ProjectMemberModel) {\n126:                         persister = new ModelMemberFilePersister();\n127:                     }\n128:                     persister.save(projectMember, writer, null);\n129:                 }\n130:             }\n131: \n132:             // if save did not raise an exception\n133:             // and name+\"#\" exists move name+\"#\" to name+\"~\"\n134:             // this is the correct backup file\n135:             if (lastArchiveFile.exists()) {\n136:                 lastArchiveFile.delete();\n137:             }\n138:             if (tempFile.exists() && !lastArchiveFile.exists()) {\n139:                 tempFile.renameTo(lastArchiveFile);\n140:             }\n141:             if (tempFile.exists()) {\n142:                 tempFile.delete();\n143:             }\n144:         } catch (Exception e) {\n145:             LOG.error(\"Exception occured during save attempt\", e);\n146:             try {\n147:                 writer.close();\n148:             } catch (IOException ex) { }\n149: \n150:             // frank: in case of exception\n151:             // delete name and mv name+\"#\" back to name if name+\"#\" exists\n152:             // this is the \"rollback\" to old file\n153:             file.delete();\n154:             tempFile.renameTo(file);\n155:             // we have to give a message to user and set the system to unsaved!\n156:             throw new SaveException(e);\n157:         }\n158: \n159:         try {\n160:             writer.close();\n161:         } catch (IOException ex) {\n162:             LOG.error(\"Failed to close save output writer\", ex);\n163:         }\n164:     }\n165: \n166: \n167:     /**\n168:      * This method creates a project from the specified URL\n169:      *\n170:      * Unlike the constructor which forces an .argo extension This\n171:      * method will attempt to load a raw XMI file\n172:      *\n173:      * This method can fail in several different ways. Either by\n174:      * throwing an exception or by having the\n175:      * ArgoParser.SINGLETON.getLastLoadStatus() set to not true.\n176:      *\n177:      * @param url The URL to load the project from.\n178:      * @return The newly loaded project.\n179:      * @throws OpenException if the file can not be opened\n180:      *\n181:      * @see org.argouml.persistence.ProjectFilePersister#doLo